  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q1",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "A horizontal drainpipe $6$ m above sea level empties storm water horizontally into the sea. The water reaches the sea $2$ m from the pipe. Find the initial speed to 1 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1.8\\ \\text{m s}^{-1}$",
      "worked": "Take the pipe as the origin, with upward positive. Since $\\theta=0^\\circ$,\n$$y=-5t^2,\\qquad x=Vt.$$\nAt sea level, $y=-6$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5t^2&=-6\\\\t&=\\sqrt{\\frac65}\\ \\text{s}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $x=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=V\\sqrt{\\frac65}\\\\V&=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6/5}}\\\\V&\\approx1.8\\ \\text{m s}^{-1}\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
